# Local attempt

Import Conventions from "./conventions.lg".
Import HostFiles from "./host_files.lg".
Import HostTools from "./host_tools.lg".
Import NodeRecord from "./node_record.lg".
Import WorkRecord from "./work_record.lg".
Import VerdictRecord from "./verdict_record.lg".
Import TrailRecord from "./trail_record.lg".
Import TrailMemory from "./trail_memory.lg".
Import AttemptRecord from "./attempt_record.lg".
Import Extraction from "./extraction.lg".
Import VernacularCommand from "./vernacular_command.lg".
Import SubmissionPolicy from "./submission_policy.lg".
Import Verifier from "./verifier.lg".
Import LocalStore from "./local_store.lg".

What one answer comes to: the submission taken out of it, the approach it takes,
the kernel's verdict — skipped when the same approach already failed on this
statement — and every artifact stored under its hash.

## A Judged has:
    a verdict, which is Verdict.
    a fingerprint, which is Text.
    a documentSha, which is Text.
    an artifacts, which is Seq of Text.
    an extraction, which is Extraction.

## To judgeAnswer (workspace: Text, statement: Statement, kind: Text, strategyId: Text, trail: Seq of TrailEntry, content: Text) -> Judged:
    Let x be extractSubmission(content).
    Let mutable j be a new Judged with verdict refusedSubmissionVerdict([x's problem]) and fingerprint "" and documentSha "" and artifacts [] and extraction x.
    Set j's fingerprint to approachFingerprint(kind, statement's sha256, strategyId, "no-submission").
    If x's problem is not equal to "":
        Return j.
    Set j's fingerprint to approachFingerprint(kind, statement's sha256, strategyId, submissionSkeleton(x's block)).
    Let document be assembleProofDocument(statement's document, x's block, proofNameFor(statement's goalName)).
    Set j's documentSha to storeArtifact(workspace, document).
    Set j's artifacts to ["submission:" + storeArtifact(workspace, x's block), "document:" + j's documentSha].
    If fingerprintFailed(trail, j's fingerprint):
        Set j's verdict to refusedSubmissionVerdict(["this approach already failed on this statement (fingerprint " + j's fingerprint + ")"]).
        Return j.
    Set j's verdict to judgeSubmission(defaultToolchain(), statement's document, statement's goalName, x's block).
    Return j.

## Note
The diagnostics a trail entry records: the refused block and the kernel's error
(or the refusal), then the policy's reason.

## To verdictDiagnostics (v: Verdict) -> Text:
    If v's kind is equal to "verified":
        Return "".
    If v's block is greater than 0:
        Return "block {v's block}: " + v's error + "\n" + v's detail.
    Return v's error + "\n" + v's detail.

## Note
The exit code an entry records: 0 the kernel checked, 1 refused, 2 infrastructure.

## To verdictExit (v: Verdict) -> Int:
    If v's kind is equal to "verified" or v's kind is equal to "admitted_axiom":
        Return 0.
    If v's kind is equal to "rejected":
        Return 1.
    Return 2.

## Note
The trail entry an attempt adds.

## To attemptEntry (e: TrailEntry, j: Judged, costMicros: Int, promptArtifacts: Seq of Text) -> TrailEntry:
    Let mutable out be e.
    Set out's approachFingerprint to j's fingerprint.
    Set out's artifactShas to promptArtifacts + j's artifacts.
    Set out's verdict to j's verdict's kind.
    Set out's exitCode to verdictExit(j's verdict).
    Set out's diagnostics to verdictDiagnostics(j's verdict).
    Set out's costMicros to costMicros.
    Set out's summary to j's extraction's summary.
    Set out's nextSuggestions to j's extraction's suggestions.
    Return out.

## Note
Everything an attempt writes: its trail line, its attempt line, the dead end of a
refused approach, and a verified proof with its verdict in the results.

## To recordAttempt (workspace: Text, resultsDir: Text, entry: TrailEntry, attempt: Attempt, j: Judged) -> Text:
    Let slug be slugOf(entry's problemId).
    Let a be appendLine(workspace + "/trails", slug + ".jsonl", toJson_TrailEntry(entry)).
    Let b be appendLine(workspace + "/attempts", slug + ".jsonl", toJson_Attempt(attempt)).
    If j's verdict's kind is equal to "rejected" and j's extraction's problem is equal to "":
        Let c be appendLine(workspace + "/dead-ends", slug + ".txt", j's fingerprint).
    If j's verdict's kind is equal to "verified":
        Let made be ensureDir(resultsDir + "/" + slug).
        Inspect readText(workspace + "/artifacts/" + j's documentSha + ".txt"):
            When Ok (doc):
                Let d be writeAtomically(resultsDir + "/" + slug + "/" + j's documentSha + ".kernel", doc).
            When Err (e):
                Return "the verified document is missing: " + e.
        Let v be writeAtomically(resultsDir + "/" + slug + "/" + j's documentSha + ".verdict.json", toJson_Verdict(j's verdict)).
    Return "".
